VeridianOS: collation: do not read builder data before it is constructed

Backport of upstream ICU commit 45a8a28de6f (ICU-22779, ICU 79.1; drop
this patch when moving to ICU 79). GCC reported, in the
DataBuilderCollationIterator constructor (i18n/collationdatabuilder.cpp,
inlined from the CollationIterator constructor in
i18n/collationiterator.h): "'...CollationData::trie' is used
uninitialized [-Wuninitialized]".

Real (latent) undefined behaviour: the base class CollationIterator is
initialized before the member builderData, but it is passed &builderData
and its constructor read d->trie, an indeterminate value. Upstream adds a
protected constructor that takes the trie explicitly (nullptr: the
builder's data has no trie of its own), which DataBuilderCollationIterator
uses. Every other CollationIterator subclass is unaffected.

--- a/i18n/collationdatabuilder.cpp
+++ b/i18n/collationdatabuilder.cpp
@@ -164,7 +164,7 @@ class DataBuilderCollationIterator : public CollationIterator {
 };
 
 DataBuilderCollationIterator::DataBuilderCollationIterator(CollationDataBuilder &b)
-        : CollationIterator(&builderData, /*numeric=*/ false),
+        : CollationIterator(&builderData, /*nullTrie=*/ nullptr, /*numeric=*/ false),
           builder(b), builderData(b.nfcImpl),
           s(nullptr), pos(0) {
     builderData.base = builder.base;
--- a/i18n/collationiterator.h
+++ b/i18n/collationiterator.h
@@ -212,6 +212,22 @@ class U_I18N_API_CLASS CollationIterator : public UObject {
 protected:
     CollationIterator(const CollationIterator &other);
 
+    /**
+     * A special constructor used by DataBuilderCollationIterator, which initializes
+     * the CollationData in the constructor. The public CollationIterator constructor
+     * initializes the trie pointer from the CollationData, but it's not yet available
+     * when DataBuilderCollationIterator invokes the CollationIterator constructor.
+     * The CollationData used by DataBuilderCollationIterator is the Normalizer2Impl,
+     * which does not have a trie, so the trie pointer is set to nullptr.
+     */
+    CollationIterator(const CollationData *d, std::nullptr_t nullTrie, UBool numeric)
+            : trie(nullTrie),
+              data(d),
+              cesIndex(0),
+              skipped(nullptr),
+              numCpFwd(-1),
+              isNumeric(numeric) {}
+
     void reset();
 
     /**
